next one, I added a "favourite" heart on each card. I put the state inside Card:

```jsx
function Card({ project }) {
  const [fav, setFav] = useState(false);
  return (
    <div className="card">
      <img src={project.thumb} />
      <h3>{project.title}</h3>
      <button onClick={() => setFav(!fav)}>{fav ? '♥' : '♡'}</button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

but when I filter and the card disappears and comes back, the heart resets. and I want to show a "favourites only" toggle too

turns.assistant:
Both problems have the same cause: the favourite state lives inside `Card`, so it's lost when the card unmounts (filtered out), and `Gallery` can't see it to filter.

The fix is to **lift the state up** to `Gallery`:

```jsx
// in Gallery
const [favs, setFavs] = useState(new Set());
const [favsOnly, setFavsOnly] = useState(false);

const toggleFav = id => {
  setFavs(prev => {
    const next = new Set(prev);
    next.has(id) ? next.delete(id) : next.add(id);
    return next;
  });
};

const filtered = projects.filter(p =>
  (category === 'all' || p.category === category) &&
  p.title.toLowerCase().includes(search.toLowerCase()) &&
  (!favsOnly || favs.has(p.id))
);

// render
<Card key={p.id} project={p} isFav={favs.has(p.id)} onToggleFav={() => toggleFav(p.id)} />
```

Then `Card` becomes stateless and just uses `isFav` and `onToggleFav` props. Note that a new `Set` is created each time, since React only re-renders when it sees a new object.

Yes, that's a standard approach. Two details to get right:

1. **Sets don't serialise to JSON** directly, so convert to an array.
2. **Load initial state with a lazy initializer**, so you read localStorage only once and avoid a flash of empty favourites:

```jsx
const [favs, setFavs] = useState(() => {
  try {
    const saved = localStorage.getItem('favs');
    return new Set(saved ? JSON.parse(saved) : []);
  } catch {
    return new Set();
  }
});

useEffect(() => {
  try {
    localStorage.setItem('favs', JSON.stringify([...favs]));
  } catch {}
}, [favs]);
```

The try/catch covers private browsing modes or blocked storage, where localStorage can throw. This is a good use of `useEffect`: syncing state to something outside React, unlike the earlier filtering case.
